                {
                  "text": "The Dorgeshuun civil war.",
                  "steps": [
                    {
                      "player": "Can you tell me about the Dorgeshuun civil war?"
                    },
                    {
                      "npc": "Certainly!  *Ahem*"
                    },
                    {
                      "npc": "At first, Dorgesh-Kaan was ruled over by generals, just as the tribe had been when it was on the surface. Each general succeeded the last by defeating him in combat."
                    },
                    {
                      "npc": "The generals were advised by a council of elders, but the Dorgeshuun were no longer an army, and many of the people felt that the Council should have authority."
                    },
                    {
                      "npc": "The people voted to become a republic, but General Bonehelm refused to give up power, and so the Dorgeshuun Civil War began."
                    },
                    {
                      "npc": "The republican faction was larger, but the military faction contained most of the trained warriors and controlled the magical equipment that the tribe had brought from the surface."
                    },
                    {
                      "npc": "General Bonehelm was driven from the city, but dug his own base out of the caves nearby."
                    },
                    {
                      "npc": "General Bonehelm's army attacked the city using archers mounted on giant frogs. There was a bloody battle, and General Bonehelm was driven back again into his base."
                    },
                    {
                      "npc": "But General Bonehelm's mining had weakened the stone around his base, and the retreating army's footsteps caused the roof to collapse, crushing his army."
                    },
                    {
                      "npc": "That was the last time one Dorgeshuun has raised arms against another. Since then, the city has been ruled peacefully by an elected council."
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "Recent years.",
                  "steps": [
                    {
                      "player": "Can you tell me about recent years?"
                    },
                    {
                      "npc": "Ah, this is where you come in!  *Ahem*"
                    },
                    {
                      "npc": "In the twenty-ninth century since the founding of the city, one of the miners broke through a wall into the cellar of a surface dwelling. The miners blocked up the tunnel and went back into their mines."
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "condition",
                      "text": "If the player has described themself as a human:",
                      "steps": [
